# tdsmap.ref - Golden MODX -> dispatch-target catalog for PROGRAM TDSMAP
#
# Source of truth: FROZEN mis/xsem00.f OSCAR computed-GO TO dispatch
#   ladder (read-only). MODX extracted by xsem00 at L182:
#   MODX = RSHIFT(INOSCR(3),16); the modern dispatcher receives MODX
#   as a passed argument and must resolve each MODX to the SAME
#   target catalogued below.
#
# Format: each data line is  "<MODX> <TARGET>"  (integer then one
#   token).
#   <TARGET> = dispatched subroutine name, OR
#              CONTINUE  for a reserved no-op slot, OR
#              FATAL     for an in-range slot that falls through to
#              GO TO 940.
# Lines beginning with '#' and blank lines are ignored by the driver
#   tdsmap.f.
#
# Totals: TOTAL=217  CALL=193  DISTINCT=188  RESERVED=21  FATAL=3
#   RANGE=1..217
#   (XCEI is shared by 6 MODX values 5,6,7,11,12,13 => 193 calls,
#    188 distinct.)
#   Reserved no-op MODX (21): 25 36 41 49 61 74 84 94 102 113 123 132
#                             140 143 153 157 163 172 187 202 213
#   In-range fatal MODX (3):  1 2 4
#   MODX 43 -> EMG (special: LINKNO=LINKNM(8) swap, then CALL EMG,
#              then restore; the dispatched target subroutine name
#              is EMG).
#
# EXPECT_VERDICT PASS: TDSMAP
#
